* IF.COM - EXTENDED CONDITION TESTS

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* IF.COM - EXTENDED CONDITION TESTS

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:IF condition arguments
    SYSUTLS:IF argument1=argument2
    SYSUTLS:IF register-number [value]

Provides the extended Z-System IF tests. The resident flow processor can
delegate tests that it does not implement to this program. Only the first
two letters of a condition name are significant. A leading ~ negates
conditions except the argument1=argument2 form.

Supported names printed by this binary include EXIST, EMPTY, ERROR, NULL,
INPUT, REG, WHEEL, TCAP, ARCHIVE, RO, SYS, AMBIG, COMPR, VALUE and ZEX,
plus comparison operators.

A condition starts a flow level; balance it with FI. Use HELP IF for the
resident forms and flow-control commands. The disk-based extended test
utility is private in this installation.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
